  "full_response": "A week-long global internet shutdown would have **catastrophic and far-reaching consequences** across nearly every aspect of modern society. Here’s a breakdown of the potential impacts:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Economic Collapse & Financial Chaos**\n- **Stock Markets Crash**: Global exchanges (NYSE, NASDAQ, LSE, Nikkei, etc.) rely on real-time digital trading. A shutdown would halt trading, causing panic, liquidity freezes, and massive losses.\n- **Banking & Payments Freeze**:\n  - ATMs, credit/debit cards, and digital wallets (PayPal, Venmo, Apple Pay) would fail.\n  - Online banking and wire transfers would stop, stranding people without cash.\n  - Cryptocurrencies (Bitcoin, Ethereum) would become inaccessible, as exchanges and wallets require internet access.\n- **Supply Chain Breakdown**:\n  - Just-in-time manufacturing (e.g., automotive, electronics) would halt due to disrupted logistics tracking.\n  - Grocery stores and pharmacies would face shortages as inventory systems fail.\n  - Fuel pumps (many require digital authorization) and air traffic control systems could malfunction.\n- **Businesses Collapse**:\n  - E-commerce (Amazon, Alibaba, Shopify) would grind to a halt.\n  - Remote work would become impossible, crippling productivity.\n  - Small businesses relying on digital payments or cloud services would suffer immediate losses.\n\n**Estimated Global GDP Loss**: **$10–$20 trillion** (based on past regional outages and economic models).\n\n---\n\n### **2. Communication & Social Disruption**\n- **No Calls/Texts**: VoIP (WhatsApp, Zoom, Skype) and even traditional phone networks (which rely on internet backbones) would fail.\n- **Social Media Blackout**: No Twitter, Facebook, Instagram, or TikTok—cutting off news, coordination, and misinformation alike.\n- **Emergency Services Overwhelmed**:\n  - 911 (US), 112 (EU), 999 (UK), and other emergency could fail or become jammed.\n  - Hospitals would struggle with digital records, telemedicine, and equipment reliant on cloud connectivity.\n- **Misinformation & Panic**:\n  - Without verified news, rumors would spread via word of mouth, SMS (if available), or radio.\n  - Governments might struggle to disseminate official updates.\n\n---\n\n### **",
